Anteater Poker — Alpha Release
Team 23 | EECS 22L | University of California, Irvine
Version: Alpha  |  Date: May 2026

AUTHORS
-------
Team 23 — EECS 22L Spring 2026, UCI

DESCRIPTION
-----------
Anteater Poker is an online multiplayer Texas Hold'em variant featuring
the UCI Anteater Wild Card mechanic. Players connect to a central server,
choose a seat, and play against other humans or bots using a GTK3 GUI.

QUICK START
-----------
See INSTALL for full build instructions.

  1. Start the server:
       poker/bin/poker_server &

  2. Launch one or more clients:
       poker/bin/poker_client

  3. On the login screen, enter your username, the server IP, and port
     (default: 127.0.0.1:9000), then click "Connect & Join Game".

  4. The server dashboard allows adding bots and dealing new hands.

ANTEATER WILD CARD RULE
-----------------------
One player per round is randomly dealt the Anteater Wild Card (🐜).
The Wild Card can substitute for any rank or suit to form the best
possible 5-card hand. If the Wild Card is used in the winning hand,
the winner receives a bonus of 200 points on top of the pot.

For full rules and user manual, see:
  poker/doc/Poker_UserManual.pdf

For software architecture details, see:
  poker/doc/Poker_SoftwareSpec.pdf
